## R2 + R6 implementation log
Date: 2026-04-26
Items: R2 (Punycode-aware identifier emitter) + R6 (stdlib type short forms)

## Files modified

- scheme/swift/stable/remangler.go
    - Updated package doc comment (added Punycode.cpp ref)
    - Added `stdlibKey` type and `reverseStdlib` map (package-level vars)
    - Added `init()` that populates reverseStdlib via EachStdlibSubstitution +
      EachStdlibSubstitution2
    - Replaced stub `mangleIdentifier` with three-path implementation:
        empty → "0", non-ASCII → "00<len><punycode>", ASCII → "<len><text>"
    - Extended `mangleNominal` with stdlib fast-path via `stdlibToken()`
    - Added `stdlibToken()` helper (reverse-map lookup)

- scheme/swift/common/substitution.go
    - Added exported `StdlibEntry{Module, Name string}` struct
    - Added `EachStdlibSubstitution(fn)` iterator over StdlibSubstitutions
    - Added `EachStdlibSubstitution2(fn)` iterator over StdlibSubstitutions2
    (These let remanglers build reverse maps without re-exporting the
    unexported `stdlib` type.)

- scheme/swift/stable/remangler_test.go
    - Added TestRemangleNonASCII: tree with Identifier("café") →
      expected "$s1M007caf_dmaV"; also verifies demangler can parse output
    - Added TestRemangleEmptyIdentifier: Identifier("") → "$s0"
    - Added TestRemangleNonASCIIPunyError: invalid-UTF-8 identifier →
      ErrUnsupported (PunycodeEncode fails with errPunycodeInvalidUTF8)
    - Added TestRemangleStdlibShortForms: spot-checks Si, Sa, ScC, Sb, SS
    - Added TestRemangleStdlibRoundTrip: $sSi, $sSa, $sScC, $sSS demangle
      then remangle back to original

