## Remangler.cpp line references used

- mangleIdentifierImpl (line 437–446): length-prefix + punycode dispatch
- ManglingUtils.h mangleIdentifier (line 127–244): "00" prefix for
  non-ASCII identifiers, zero-length special "0" form
- Punycode.cpp encodePunycodeUTF8 (called by mangleIdentifierImpl):
  UTF-8 → Apple-variant punycode, output wrapped in 00<len><encoded>
- Remangler::mangleAnyNominalType (line 547–593): stdlib-substitution
  check before emitting full module+identifier+trailer form

## Known gaps still remaining

- R3: Word-substitution emission (0<letter>…) — identifiers that share
  suffixes are not compressed; each gets full length-prefix form.
- R4: Node-level back-substitutions (A0_, A1_, …) — not emitted.
- R5: Bound-generic nominal remangle (Sa y Si G etc.) — BoundGenericStructure
  not yet in remangleNode dispatch.
- All remaining node kinds (Function, FunctionType, Tuple, Metatype, …)
  return ErrUnsupported.
- Round-trip for symbols containing unicode identifiers is one-directional:
  tree("café") → "$s1M007caf_dmaV" → demangled-tree("caf_dma") ≠ original.
  Full round-trip requires the demangler to decode punycode in the $s path
  (currently documented as intentionally omitted per stable.go comment).
